IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coroners-dates`

-- Coroners Act 1997 (Australian Capital Territory) -- from the seat of the owner or occupier of property: property
-- destroyed or damaged by a fire (Division 3.2 inquiries), or a place a coroner's search warrant (s 66) or coronial
-- investigation scene order (Part 5A) reaches. A fire inquiry's findings on cause and origin often matter to an insurance
-- or damages claim.
--
-- "Must there be an inquiry into the fire that damaged my house? If I ask for one and the coroner says no, what must I be
-- told? Can I get the findings? A warrant was executed at my place: must I see it, and is it still in force? My property
-- has been made a coronial investigation scene: for how long?"
--
-- The Act's provisions are addressed to coroners and police; they are encoded as what they mean for the owner or
-- occupier. Every opinion or satisfaction of an official is asked as an input. The family member's seat is
-- coroners-family.l4 (its s 64, s 67 and s 90 to 93 questions apply to fire inquiries too); the witness's seat is
-- coroners-witness.l4. Names here are this module's own.
--
-- Edition: Republication No 51 (R51), effective 5 September 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/A1997-57.txt.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.
