§ `Coroners Act 1997 (ACT) -- the owner or occupier of property`

§§ `ss 18, 54(2) -- an inquiry into a fire (only if my property was destroyed or damaged by fire)`

-- s 18(1): "A coroner must hold an inquiry into the cause and origin of a fire that has destroyed or damaged property if
-- asked to do so by the Attorney-General." (2): "A coroner may (at the request of the owner or occupier of destroyed or
-- damaged property or on the coroner's own initiative) hold an inquiry into the cause and origin of a fire if the coroner
-- considers that an inquiry should be held." (3): where the owner or occupier asks and "the coroner is of the opinion
-- that an inquiry into the cause and origin of the fire should not be held; the coroner must give to each owner or
-- occupier who requested that an inquiry be held written notice of the opinion and the grounds for the opinion."
DECLARE `Fire inquiry answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Attorney-General has asked, so a coroner must hold an inquiry into the cause and origin of the fire (s 18(1))`
    `possibly: the coroner considers an inquiry should be held, and may hold one at my request or on the coroner's own initiative (s 18(2)); it is a discretion`
    `no: the coroner is of the opinion that no inquiry should be held, and must give me written notice of that opinion and its grounds (s 18(3))`
    `not unless the Attorney-General asks or the coroner considers an inquiry should be held; as owner or occupier I may ask for one (s 18(2))`

@export Must there be a coroner's inquiry into the fire that destroyed or damaged my property?
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has asked for an inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Attorney-General has asked a coroner to hold an inquiry into the fire
      `I have asked for an inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as owner or occupier of the destroyed or damaged property, have asked a coroner to hold an inquiry
      `the coroner considers an inquiry should be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner considers that an inquiry into the cause and origin of the fire should be held
GIVETH A `Fire inquiry answer`
DECIDE `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` IS
    IF `the Attorney-General has asked for an inquiry`
    THEN `yes: the Attorney-General has asked, so a coroner must hold an inquiry into the cause and origin of the fire (s 18(1))`
    ELSE IF `the coroner considers an inquiry should be held`
         THEN `possibly: the coroner considers an inquiry should be held, and may hold one at my request or on the coroner's own initiative (s 18(2)); it is a discretion`
         ELSE IF `I have asked for an inquiry`
              THEN `no: the coroner is of the opinion that no inquiry should be held, and must give me written notice of that opinion and its grounds (s 18(3))`
              ELSE `not unless the Attorney-General asks or the coroner considers an inquiry should be held; as owner or occupier I may ask for one (s 18(2))`

-- s 54(2): "A coroner holding an inquiry into a fire must, on the request of the owner of the property damaged or
-- destroyed by the fire, make available a copy of the coroner's findings to the owner." An occupier is not named
-- (finding 10).
DECLARE `Fire findings answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have asked, and the coroner must make a copy of the findings available to me as owner (s 54(2))`
    `yes, if I ask: on my request as owner the coroner must make a copy of the findings available to me (s 54(2))`
    `not covered: s 54(2) gives a copy to the owner of the property; an occupier who is not the owner is not named`

@export Can I get a copy of the coroner's findings on the fire?
GIVEN `I own the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the property the fire damaged or destroyed (rather than only occupying it, for example as a tenant)
      `I have asked for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the coroner for a copy of the findings
GIVETH A `Fire findings answer`
DECIDE `Can I get a copy of the fire findings question` IS
    IF (NOT `I own the property`)
    THEN `not covered: s 54(2) gives a copy to the owner of the property; an occupier who is not the owner is not named`
    ELSE IF `I have asked for a copy`
         THEN `yes: I have asked, and the coroner must make a copy of the findings available to me as owner (s 54(2))`
         ELSE `yes, if I ask: on my request as owner the coroner must make a copy of the findings available to me (s 54(2))`

§§ `s 66 -- a search warrant at my place (only if a coroner's warrant reaches it)`

-- s 66(4): "A warrant must-- ... (d) specify the date, being a date not later than 1 month after the date of issue of the
-- warrant, on which the warrant ceases to have effect." (5): "A warrant may be executed, in accordance with its terms, at
-- any time during the period commencing on the date of issue of the warrant and ending at the expiration of the date
-- specified for the purpose of subsection (4) (d)." (6): "Before exercising a power under a warrant, the person executing
-- the warrant must give a copy of the warrant to the owner or occupier of the place to which it relates."
DECLARE `Warrant copy answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: before exercising any power under the warrant, the person executing it must give me, as owner or occupier, a copy of it (s 66(6))`
    `the person executing the warrant has not done what s 66(6) requires: a copy must be given to the owner or occupier before any power under it is exercised`

@export A coroner's search warrant is being executed at my place. Must I be given a copy?
GIVEN `I was given a copy before any power was exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a copy of the warrant before the person executing it exercised any power under it
GIVETH A `Warrant copy answer`
DECIDE `Must I be given a copy of the warrant question` IS
    IF `I was given a copy before any power was exercised`
    THEN `yes: before exercising any power under the warrant, the person executing it must give me, as owner or occupier, a copy of it (s 66(6))`
    ELSE `the person executing the warrant has not done what s 66(6) requires: a copy must be given to the owner or occupier before any power under it is exercised`

DECLARE `Warrant in force answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the day is within the period from the date of issue to the end of the date stated in the warrant (s 66(5))`
    `no: the warrant has ceased to have effect at the end of the date stated in it (s 66(4)(d), (5))`
    `no: the warrant could not yet be executed, as the day is before its date of issue (s 66(5))`
    `the warrant does not meet s 66(4)(d): the date it states for ceasing to have effect is more than 1 month after its date of issue`

@export Is the coroner's search warrant for my place still in force on a given day?
GIVEN `the date of issue` IS A DATE @desc The warrant's date of issue (ISO 8601)
      `the date it ceases to have effect` IS A DATE @desc The date the warrant states as the date it ceases to have effect (ISO 8601)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Warrant in force answer`
DECIDE `Is the warrant in force question` IS
    IF (NOT (`the date it ceases to have effect` `is on or before` (1 `months after` `the date of issue`)))
    THEN `the warrant does not meet s 66(4)(d): the date it states for ceasing to have effect is more than 1 month after its date of issue`
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the date of issue` `is on or before` `the day in question`))
         THEN `no: the warrant could not yet be executed, as the day is before its date of issue (s 66(5))`
         ELSE IF `the day in question` `is on or before` `the date it ceases to have effect`
              THEN `yes: the day is within the period from the date of issue to the end of the date stated in the warrant (s 66(5))`
              ELSE `no: the warrant has ceased to have effect at the end of the date stated in it (s 66(4)(d), (5))`

§§ `Part 5A -- my property as a coronial investigation scene (only if a scene order or declaration covers it)`

-- s 68C(2): "A coronial investigation scene order-- (a) may be issued at any time before the end of an inquest or
-- inquiry; and (b) must state-- (i) the date and time the order is issued; and (ii) the date, within 30 days after the
-- order was made, the order ends; and (iii) any conditions applying under the order." (3): "A coroner may, before a
-- coronial investigation order ends (a current order), order an extension of the current order for an additional period
-- (an extension period) if-- (a) the date the extension period ends is within 30 days after the day the current order
-- ends; and (b) the coroner is satisfied that an extension of the current order is in the interests of justice." (4): an
-- extension may be ordered more than once.
-- s 68F(3)(b): a senior police officer's declaration (made when no coroner is available) "ends when whichever of the
-- following happens first: (i) a coronial investigation order is issued for the place; (ii) the period of 24 hours after
-- the declaration was made ends".
-- s 68E lists the powers at a scene: directing people and vehicles to leave, searching, opening locked things, taking
-- utilities, seizing things, digging up anything, removing wall or ceiling linings, floors or vehicle panels, and more.
DECLARE `Scene order answer` IS ONE OF
    `the order's end date is within the limit: no later than 30 days after the order was made (s 68C(2)(b)(ii))`
    `the order does not meet s 68C(2)(b)(ii): its end date is more than 30 days after the order was made`

@export My property has been made a coronial investigation scene. Is the end date in the order within the Act's limit?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the coronial investigation scene order was made (ISO 8601)
      `the day the order ends` IS A DATE @desc The end date stated in the order (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Scene order answer`
DECIDE `Is the scene order end date lawful question` IS
    IF `the day the order ends` `is on or before` (30 `days after` `the day the order was made`)
    THEN `the order's end date is within the limit: no later than 30 days after the order was made (s 68C(2)(b)(ii))`
    ELSE `the order does not meet s 68C(2)(b)(ii): its end date is more than 30 days after the order was made`

DECLARE `Scene extension answer` IS ONE OF
    `an extension may run to` HAS `the latest day` IS A DATE
    `no extension: the coroner may extend the order only if satisfied that an extension is in the interests of justice (s 68C(3)(b))`
    `no extension: an extension must be ordered before the current order ends (s 68C(3))`

@export The coronial investigation scene order on my property may be extended. How long can an extension run?
GIVEN `the day the current order ends` IS A DATE @desc The date the current order (or its latest extension) ends (ISO 8601)
      `the coroner is satisfied an extension is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner is satisfied that extending the order is in the interests of justice
      `the extension was ordered before the current order ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the extension is ordered before the current order ends
GIVETH A `Scene extension answer`
DECIDE `Latest end of a scene extension question` IS
    IF (NOT `the extension was ordered before the current order ended`)
    THEN `no extension: an extension must be ordered before the current order ends (s 68C(3))`
    ELSE IF (NOT `the coroner is satisfied an extension is in the interests of justice`)
         THEN `no extension: the coroner may extend the order only if satisfied that an extension is in the interests of justice (s 68C(3)(b))`
         ELSE `an extension may run to` (30 `days after` `the day the current order ends`)

DECLARE `Scene declaration answer` IS ONE OF
    `the declaration has ended: a coronial investigation scene order has been issued for the place (s 68F(3)(b)(i)); the order now governs`
    `the declaration is in force, for at most 24 hours from when it was made (s 68F(3)(b)(ii))`
    `the declaration has ended: 24 hours have passed since it was made (s 68F(3)(b)(ii))`

@export A senior police officer declared my property a coronial investigation scene. Is the declaration still in force?
GIVEN `hours since the declaration was made` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours have passed since the senior police officer made the declaration
      `a coroner has since issued a scene order for the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coroner has since issued a coronial investigation scene order for the place
GIVETH A `Scene declaration answer`
DECIDE `Is the police scene declaration in force question` IS
    IF `a coroner has since issued a scene order for the place`
    THEN `the declaration has ended: a coronial investigation scene order has been issued for the place (s 68F(3)(b)(i)); the order now governs`
    ELSE IF `hours since the declaration was made` BELOW 24
         THEN `the declaration is in force, for at most 24 hours from when it was made (s 68F(3)(b)(ii))`
         ELSE `the declaration has ended: 24 hours have passed since it was made (s 68F(3)(b)(ii))`
